and its sign (+ or -) independently, so the hint can say Add beside a minus sign, and its second number is always 0. F12 asks for the missing fraction when counting by quarters, but its join (F18) can print zero, one or two blanks, while F16 keys a single fraction 2/4 or 3/4 chosen independently of any blank. F18 and F21 print values that are not quarters (1/2, 3/2, 4/3, 4/2), which is wrong for counting by quarters and outside scope. F20 prints the keyed answers 2/2, 2/4, 3/4 and 4/4 across items, but the quarter sequences in F05, F06, F10, F11 and F14 all end at 4/4, so a 2/4 or 3/4 key is wrong for those items. Because the answer derives only from numerator and denominator, the generator cannot tie the key to the printed sequence.\"}",
